WEBVTT

00:00:27.746 --> 00:00:30.579
the word “rabota”, in Old Church Slavonic,

00:00:30.579 --> 00:00:33.037
described the forced labor of the people.

00:00:35.204 --> 00:00:37.371
A slight change in spelling,

00:00:37.371 --> 00:00:39.829
and rabota became robota in Czech,

00:00:39.829 --> 00:00:43.162
which, in addition to defining
the toil of the serfs,

00:00:43.162 --> 00:00:44.996
was also used figuratively

00:00:44.996 --> 00:00:48.246
to describe any kind
of hard work or drudgery.

00:00:51.329 --> 00:00:55.121
In 1920, Czech writer
Karel Capek published

00:00:55.121 --> 00:00:58.621
a science fiction play called “R.U.R.“,

00:00:58.621 --> 00:01:01.912
short for “Rossum’s Universal Robots.”